{title: 528 - A Shelter in the Time of Storm}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #528 • A SHELTER IN THE TIME OF • 16.16.16.16}
{lyricist: Vernon J. Charlesworth}
{composer: EF. E. Belden}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 528}
{meta: tune A SHELTER IN THE TIME OF}
{meta: meter 16.16.16.16}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]The Lord's our Rock, [Bb/F]in [F]Him [Gm/Bb]we [Bb]hide, [Gm]A Shelter [C]in the [F/C]time of [C7]storm;
[C7/E]Secure [F]whatever may betide, [Bb/F]A Shelter [F]in [Gm/Bb]the [Bb]time of [Gm]storm.
[Gm]Mighty [C]Rock in a weary [F/C]land, Cooling shade on [C7]the burning [F]sand,
[F]Faithful guide [Bb]for the pilgrim band- [F]A shelter in the time of storm.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F]Mighty Rock in [C]a weary [F]land,
[F]Cooling shade on [Bb]the burning sand,
[Bb]Faithful [F]guide for the pilgrim band--
[C7]A shelter in [F]the time of storm.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]A shade [Bb/F]by [Gm/Bb]day, defense [C]by [F/C]night,
[C7/E]A [F]shelter in [Bb/F]the [F]time [Gm/Bb]of [Bb]storm;
[Gm]No [C]fears alarm, [F/C]no foes [C7]afright,
[F]A shelter [Bb]in [F]the time of storm.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]The raging [Gm/Bb]storms may round [C]us [F/C]beat,
[C7/E]A [F]shelter in [Bb/F]the [F]time [Gm/Bb]of [Bb]storm
[Gm]We'll [C]never [F/C]leave our safe [C7]retreat,
[F]A shelter [Bb]in [F]the time of storm.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]O Rock [Bb/F]divine, [Gm]O Refuge [F/C]dear,
[C7/E]A [F]Shelter in [Bb/F]the [F]time [Gm/Bb]of [Bb]storm;
[Gm]Be [C]Thou our [F/C]helper ever near,
[F]A Shelter [Bb]in [F]the time of storm.
{end_of_verse}
